1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,710
Locally: GET /health → 200 OK.

2
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:12,280
Remote browser: TypeError: Failed to fetch.

3
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:18,370
Connection refused — not CORS, not a 404.

4
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:25,550
127.0.0.1 means the remote machine's OWN loopback.

5
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:29,660
Nothing is listening there.

6
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:31,520
Source: import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL

7
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:42,690
Vite replaces it at build time. The bundle holds the literal URL.

8
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:51,620
Set VITE_API_BASE_URL on the static host. The host sees it.

9
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,420
The served bundle is byte-identical.

10
00:00:54,420 --> 00:01:00,030
A static host serves files; it does not rebuild them.

11
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:05,300
Rebuild with a reachable API URL.

12
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:11,440
The new bundle contains the new literal.

13
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:19,140
Retest: GET /health → 200 OK.

14
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:27,170
VITE_ values are public. Never put a secret in one.

15
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:34,410
A server environment change cannot rewrite an existing bundle.
